% Rules with three demand calls, answered through the Magic rewrite, which
% cuts each body's prefix before its second and third call into a
% supplementary predicate.  r chains three predicates read on demand, and
% hop3 calls itself three times, so its supplementary predicates sit in a
% recursive component with hop3's adornment and magic predicate.  Every
% strategy must give the answers of the whole fixed point.

e(1, 2).
e(2, 3).
e(2, 5).
e(3, 4).
e(4, 1).
e(5, 6).
e(7, 8).

a(X, Y) :- e(X, Y).
b(X, Y) :- e(X, Y).
c(X, Y) :- e(X, Y).

r(X, W) :- a(X, Y), b(Y, Z), c(Z, W).

hop3(X, Y) :- e(X, Y).
hop3(X, W) :- hop3(X, Y), hop3(Y, Z), hop3(Z, W).

r(1, W)?
r(X, 4)?
hop3(1, W)?
hop3(7, W)?
